## 2026-07-24 — repo remediation needed (found while porting recent full-server changes)

Full PHPStan run (`vendor/bin/phpstan analyse app tests --level=5`) currently returns 1000+
errors, repo-wide, predating this session. The pre-commit hook runs this over the whole
app+tests tree, so **no commit currently passes it** — today's commits used --no-verify
per explicit instruction, after each was individually verified with php -l, Pint, and the
relevant test suite by hand.

Plan, in order:

1. **Remove dead subsystems first.** Confirmed via grep that these have zero routes and
   zero callers anywhere except themselves/each other:
   - LibriVox catalog integration (models/migrations never existed in lite; already removed
     from MySqlService.php in commit b53f9f21, but LibriVoxController and
     LibriVoxApiService/LibriVoxBookAdapter are still sitting there unused)
   - Book-library CRUD in MySqlService.php / DocumentStoreServiceInterface / 
     MockDocumentStoreService: ~80 methods for authors/genres/narrators/series/book CRUD,
     library-repair-issue queue, needs-review queue, job queue. Lite's purpose is syncing
     position/stats/bookmarks by string identity, not hosting a book library — user
     confirmed this directly, and zero callers exist outside MySqlService itself.
   - Admin\BookController and friends (BookActionController, BookSearchController,
     BookFormController, BookMetadataSearchController) — zero routes reference them.
   - Skin/Theme controllers and gallery views also appear to have zero routes (grepped
     routes/web.php + routes/api.php for Skin|Theme, no matches) — worth confirming before
     deciding whether to remove or actually wire up, since SKIN_CUSTOMIZATION_SPEC.md
     suggests this was meant to be a real feature, not dead code like LibriVox/books.
   - Also check: AudibleService/AudibleApiService/GoogleBooksApiService/HardcoverService/
     OpenAudibleParser/BookImportService/BookEnrichmentService — likely all dead too
     ("no book source should be used in lite in any way" per direct instruction), but not
     yet confirmed route/caller-free the way LibriVox and book-CRUD were.

2. **Then tune phpstan.neon rule selection.** Per instruction: many of the remaining error
   types are flagging standard Laravel magic (dynamic properties, facade returns, etc.)
   that shouldn't be treated as real errors for this codebase. Review and disable/ignore
   those specific rules rather than baselining everything wholesale.

3. **Then clean up whatever's left**, file by file.

Do NOT bulk-add everything to phpstan-baseline.neon as a shortcut — that hides real bugs
along with noise. Fix the dead-code and rule-tuning issues first; only baseline what's left
after that, and only with explicit sign-off.

